# The Baron headless driver keeps medals inert and reports spawned escorts

`HeadlessContractSim` now runs `e1-baron` through the production `WaveSystem`,
`CombatSystem`, and `RunManager`: the 1.15x cadence, wave-20 Baron and escorts,
rocket telegraph/volleys, defeat secure, and 2x science payout all come from the
contract's `twist.baron` block.

The headless host supplies no-op meta storage and never calls
`awardBaronMedal`. Its defeat transcript states that the medal is eligible but
`awarded: false` and `sideEffects: false`; a fake global `localStorage` records
zero writes.

The `WaveSystem` Baron-spawn callback now reports the number of escorts that
actually spawned. This matters at the shared alive cap: a saturated run can
force the Baron in while rejecting all eight escorts. The transcript records
zero in that case instead of echoing the declaration as if it ran.

Five pinned seeds secure at wave 20 with hashes `b9566c6d`, `5f9fd39f`,
`660091a6`, `8d4b75d1`, and `40ddab2e`, at 4.11–4.38 waves/second in the
measurement run. Seed 01's full proof ends at 528.433 seconds with 869 kills.

Related: [[The Claim headless driver posts through RunManager — 2026-08-02]] · [[GR-SIM reuses production Dry Gulch systems without a renderer — 20260730-1514]] · [[MOCs/Gold Rush MOC]]
